Let $\gamma_*=4616733319001/10^{14}$. For every $0<\gamma<\gamma_*$ there is $q_\gamma$ such that $$\label{eq:accepted-fock-gap}
 H_q^2\ge\gamma H_q\qquad(q\ge q_\gamma)$$ on all of $\mathcal F_q$. In particular, for all sufficiently large $N$ and $q=3(N-1)$, $$\label{eq:accepted-filled-gap}
 H_{N,q}\ge\frac1{25}(I-P_{N,q}).$$

If <a href="#eq:local-core-tail" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:local-core-tail">[eq:local-core-tail]</a> holds with $r\geq1$, there is a decomposition $A=\sum_{
u\geq0}A_
u$ with $A_
