u\|
       \leq C_Ba r^B.
 \label{eq:local-core-moment}$$

Let $K$ be self-adjoint and even, with a rapidly local interaction of uniform size. Write $\tau_t^K(A)=e^{itK}Ae^{-itK}$. For each $D$ there are $D'$ and $M_D$, independent of volume, such that $$\|\tau_t^K(A)\|_{x,D}
       \leq C_D(1+|t|)^{M_D}\|A\|_{x,D'}.
 \label{eq:polynomial-propagation}$$ The assertion holds also for time-dependent generators with the same uniform bounds. In particular evolution over a bounded parameter interval preserves rapid locality. If $A$ is supported in $B_r(x)$, the error in approximating $\tau_t^K(A)$ on $B_R(x)$, for $R\geq C(r+(1+|t|)^4)$, is bounded by $C_D\|A\|(1+r)^2R^{-D}$.

With $m=b/2$ and $w=w_q(m)$, the zero-extended coefficients satisfy $$|\Delta_i^r\Delta_b^s a_b(i)|
 \leq C_{D,r,s}w^{-1/2-r-s}
       \left(1+ rac{|i-m|}{w}ight)^{-D}.
 \label{eq:pair-row-symbols}$$ There are pair annihilators $L_{
u,\phi}$, rapidly local with uniform bounds about centers $x_{
u,\phi}$, and a measure $d\mu$ of bounded mass per unit ball, such that $$H_q=\sum_
u\int_0^{2\pi}
                L_{
u,\phi}^*L_{
u,\phi}\,d\mu_
u(\phi).
 \label{eq:pair-local-resolution}$$ The construction is linear in the row coefficients. In particular symbol bounds <a href="#eq:pair-row-symbols" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:pair-row-symbols">[eq:pair-row-symbols]</a> with an additional tempered factor give local bounds with that factor; the same holds for differences of row families in common frames.

Fix $p\in(0,2)$, $L\geq2$, and $f(j)=f_{L,p}(j)$. In the orthogonal coordinates <a href="#eq:flags-two-branches" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:flags-two-branches">[eq:flags-two-branches]</a>, $$\begin{split}
 (J_{q,F}\oplus J_{q,E})^*D_q(f)(J_{q,F}\oplus J_{q,E})
  ={}&\begin{pmatrix}
   D_{q-1}(f)+K_{q,1}(f)&0\\
   0&D_{q-3}(f)+f(q)+K_{q,3}(f)
  \end{pmatrix}+R_q(f),\\
 &\|R_q(f)\|\leq C_p\frac{f(q)}{(L+q)^2}.
 \end{split}
 \label{eq:flags-weighted-step}$$ The notation in the left side means the unitary whose columns are the two branch isometries. The bound includes the off-diagonal blocks. For affine $f$ the remainder is zero and $K_{q,d}(f)=0$.

There are fixed $c\geq0$ and $b_0\geq1$ with the following property. Let $O=O^*$ be neutral, of norm at most one, supported on a slot ball of radius $r\geq2$ centered at latitude index $m$, and put $u=1+m$. If $q>C r^{b_0}u$, identify all northern slots in the fluxes being compared. The two diagonal branch blocks of $O$ equal $$O+\mathcal D_{q,1}(O)\quad\hbox{and}\quad
 O+\mathcal D_{q,3}(O)$$ up to a matrix remainder of norm $C_Dq^{-D}$ for every fixed $D$. Each $\mathcal D_{q,d}(O)$ is neutral and self-adjoint. If $x$ is its original center, then, for fixed $c,C_*<\infty$ and every $D>0$, $$\begin{split}
 \|\mathcal D_{q,d}(O)\|&\leq Cr^cu/q^2,\\
 \inf_{A_R\in\mathfrak A(B_R(x))}
       \|\mathcal D_{q,d}(O)-A_R\|
  &\leq C_Dr^cu q^{-2}R^{-D}\qquad(R\geq C_*r).
 \end{split}
 \label{eq:flags-northern-size}$$ For $|q-q'|\leq2$ and fixed $d$, the difference between these changes, in common northern slots, obeys the same two estimates with $q^{-2}$ replaced by $q^{-3}$. The exponent $c$ and core constant $C_*$ are independent of $D$.

For each of $p=1/8$ and $p=3/2$ there are fixed $L\ge2$ and $c>0$ such that, for every flux and every nonzero zero-mode space $Z_{n,q}$, $$\label{eq:charge-pooled}
 \mathcal R_{n,q}\bigl(C_q(f)\mathbf1-P_{n,q}D_q(f)P_{n,q}\bigr)\mathcal R_{n,q}^*
 \ \ge\ c S_{L,p}.$$ Here compression to $Z_{n,q}$ is understood, and $P_{n,q}$ denotes its orthogonal projection. The constants are independent of $q,n$ and of the readout axis. When $h=0$, both sides vanish.

Fix $p\in(0,2)$ and a lower stopping flux $q_{\rm s}\ge8$. There is a function $\varepsilon_p(L)\to0$ as $L\to\infty$ with the following properties, uniformly for $q\ge q_{\rm s}$: $$\begin{aligned}
 \left|C_{q-1}(f)-C_q(f)+\frac13f(q)\right|
 &\le\varepsilon_p(L)f(q),\label{eq:charge-F-scalar}\\
 \sum_{q\ge q_{\rm s}}
 \frac{|\ell_q-\ell_{3\lfloor q/3\rfloor}|}{f(q)}
 &\le\varepsilon_p(L).\label{eq:charge-calibration-scalar}
\end{aligned}$$ The function $\ell$ is nonnegative. If $0<p<1$, then for every collection $\mathcal E$ of E-step fluxes along a history, and every flag position $k$ below these steps, $$\label{eq:charge-scalar-tail}
 \sum_{\substack{q\in\mathcal E\\q\ge k}}(\ell_q)_+
 \le \left(\frac{1+p}{3(1-p)}+\varepsilon_p(L)\right)f(k).$$ Changing $k$ by a fixed bounded amount, or taking $k$ in the terminal range, only changes $\varepsilon_p(L)$.

For either $p=1/8$ or $p=3/2$, as $L\to\infty$, $$\label{eq:charge-common-sums}
 \sup_{q\ge q_{\rm s}}\frac{B_q}{f(q)}=O(L^{-1}),\qquad
 \sum_{q\ge q_{\rm s}}
 \left(\frac{J_q}{f(q)}+\frac1{(L+q)^2}\right)
 =O\left(\frac{1+\log L}{L}\right).$$ For $p=1/8$ there are, in addition, $$\label{eq:charge-first-sums}
 \sum_{q\ge q_{\rm s}}
 \frac{\sup_{0\le m\le q}A_q(m)}{f(q)}=O(L^{-1}),\qquad
 \sum_{q\ge q_{\rm s}}\frac1{f(q)}
 \int_0^q\frac{A_q(m)}w\,dm=O(L^{-1/2}).$$ All implied constants are independent of $L$.

Let $W$ be a neutral Hermitian interaction with bounded strength per unit area and fixed rapid locality bounds. For unit vectors $\psi\in Z_{n,q}$ and $\chi\in Z_{n',q}$ with hole numbers $h,h'$, $$\label{eq:charge-weak-average}
 |\langle W\rangle_\psi-\langle W\rangle_\chi|
 \le C_W(q+1)^{7/8}(h+h').$$ For radius-$r$ interactions of unit local norm one can take $C_W\le C(1+r)^B$ for a fixed $B$.

There is a sequence $\varepsilon_M\to0$ such that, for every $M\ge2$ and every $q\ge30M$, $$\label{eq:evacuation-rows}
 \sum_{b=1}^{2q-1}\widetilde B_{b-1}^*\widetilde B_{b-1}
 \le\sum_{b>M}B_{b-1}^*B_{b-1}+\varepsilon_MI
 \quad\hbox{on }\mathcal F_q.$$

For $A_{q,M}$ in <a href="#eq:pair-tail-average" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:pair-tail-average">[eq:pair-tail-average]</a>, there are coefficients $0\le a_{q,M,\ell}\le1$ such that $$A_{q,M}=\sum_{\ell=0}^{2q-2}a_{q,M,\ell}P_{q,\ell}.$$ For every fixed $\ell\ge0$, $$\label{eq:spin-tail-limit}
 \lim_{M\to\infty}\limsup_{q\to\infty}a_{q,M,\ell}=0.$$ Moreover, for each fixed $\ell$ there is $C_\ell<\infty$ such that $$\label{eq:fixed-block-energy}
 \mathcal L_4(W_4P_{q,\ell}W_4^*)\le C_\ell H_q$$ for all sufficiently large $q$.

There are constants $C_{\mathrm{num}}<\infty$, $\mu>0$, $a>0$, and $C_G<\infty$, independent of sufficiently large $q=3(N-1)$, such that $$\label{eq:excess-number-bound}
 \mathcal N-N\le C_{\mathrm{num}}H_q.$$ The operator $$\label{eq:coercive-G}
 G_q=H_q+\mu(N-\mathcal N)$$ satisfies $$\label{eq:G-coercivity}
 G_q\ge a\bigl(H_q+|N-\mathcal N|\bigr)
 \ge g\bigl(I-P_{\mathrm L,N}\bigr)$$ for a constant $g>0$, with $P_{\mathrm L,N}$ extended by zero on the other Fock sectors. For every initial density matrix, the evolution <a href="#eq:loss-generator" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:loss-generator">[eq:loss-generator]</a> obeys $$\begin{aligned}
 \langle H_q\rangle_t&\le e^{-ct}\langle H_q\rangle_0,
       \label{eq:loss-energy-decay}\\
 0\le\langle\mathcal N\rangle_0-\langle\mathcal N\rangle_t
    &\le C_{\mathrm{num}}\langle H_q\rangle_0,
       \label{eq:loss-number-control}\\
 \langle G_q\rangle_t&\le C_G\langle G_q\rangle_0.
       \label{eq:loss-G-control}
\end{aligned}$$ Every limit point $\rho_\infty$ is supported on $\ker H_q$, and $$\label{eq:loss-hole-control}
 0\le\operatorname{Tr}\rho_\infty(N-\mathcal N)
       \le C_G\mu^{-1}\langle G_q\rangle_0.$$

For every fixed $0<c_0<1/25$ there exists $q_0$ such that, for every integer $q\ge q_0$, the following inequality holds on the entire Fock space $\mathcal F_q$: $$\label{rb:eq:retained-blocks}
 H_q^2\ge c_0H_q+
 \mathcal L_4\!\left(W_4R_q^{\mathrm{hi}}W_4^\dagger\right).$$ The threshold is independent of particle number.

On $\mathcal F_q$, $$\label{rb:eq:square}
 H^2=H+\mathcal L_3\!\left(W_3(W_3^\dagger W_3-I)W_3^\dagger\right)
       +\mathcal L_4(W_4W_4^\dagger).$$

The coefficient of $e_i\wedge e_j$ in $v_p$, for $i<j$, vanishes unless $i+j=p+1$, and otherwise equals $$\label{rb:eq:pair}
 v_p(i,j)=(i-j)\sqrt{\frac{(q)_i(q)_j\,p!}{q(2q-2)_p\,i!j!}}.$$ For fixed $p,i,j$, its limit is $$\label{rb:eq:pairstar}
 v_p^*(i,j)=(i-j)\sqrt{\frac{p!}{2^p i!j!}}\,\mathbf1_{i+j=p+1}.$$

$$\label{rb:eq:q}
 W_3^\dagger W_3-I=\sum_{z=0}^q q_z(q)R_{3,z},\qquad
 q_z(q)=(-1)^z\frac{(q)_z}{(2q-2)_z}
          \left(3z-1-\frac{z(z+1)}q\right).$$ In particular $W_3R_{3,z}=0$ for $z=0,1,3$ whenever these indices are allowed. For fixed $z$, $$\label{rb:eq:qlimit}
 q_z(q)\longrightarrow (3z-1)(-1/2)^z.$$

Let $W$ be a linear map between finite-dimensional Hilbert spaces, $G=W^\dagger W$, and let $C$ be self-adjoint on the domain of $W$. Then $$GCG\ge0\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad WCW^\dagger\ge0.$$ On $\mathcal F_{\mathrm{loc}}$, for any fixed finite collection $A_b=c_kc_jB(v_p^*)$ with $0\le p\le23$ and $0\le j,k\le24$, $$\label{rb:eq:annihilatorbound}
 \sum_b\lVert A_b\psi\rVert^2\le C_0\langle \psi,h_*\psi\rangle,
 \qquad h_*:=\sum_{p=0}^{23}B(v_p^*)^\dagger B(v_p^*),$$ where $C_0$ depends only on the collection.

For $q\ge24$ and $1\le D\le23$, put $$C_D^q=(d_D/d_a)\chi-E_D^q+\varepsilon I,
 \qquad h_q=\sum_{p=0}^{23}B_p^\dagger B_p.$$ Assuming <a href="#rb:eq:4certificate" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="rb:eq:4certificate">[rb:eq:4certificate]</a>, there is a scalar $\rho_q\ge0$, independent of $D$ and tending to zero as $q\to\infty$, such that $$\label{rb:eq:relative}
 \sum_{r,s\in\mathcal R_D}(C_D^q)_{rs}
 B(w_{Dr}^q)^\dagger B(w_{Ds}^q)
 \ge-\rho_qh_q$$ on the entire Fock space $\mathcal F_q$.

For the coefficients in Subsection <a href="#rb:app:certificate" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="rb:app:certificate">9.5</a>, $$\label{rb:eq:A4bound}
 A_4\le\mathcal L_4(W_4R_q^{\mathrm{lo}}W_4^\dagger)+(1222\varepsilon+o(1))H,
 \qquad q\to\infty,$$ uniformly on $\mathcal F_q$.

For sufficiently large $q$, $$\label{rb:eq:tailbound}
 \mathcal L_3\left(W_3\sum_{z=16}^q q_z(q)R_{3,z}W_3^\dagger\right)
 \ge-\delta_qH,$$ where $$\label{rb:eq:delta}
 \delta_q=\sum_{\substack{17\le z\le q\\z\text{ odd}}}
       \frac{d_{3,z}}{d_a}|q_z(q)|(z+1),\qquad
 \delta_q\longrightarrow\frac{61}{4096}.$$
